a Starts Dating Marco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Pleasant Evening", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Past & Past Continuous Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Form: subject + was/were + verb-ing </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You can use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action. The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class =\"strong\">when</span>, <span class =\"strong\">while</span> and <span class =\"strong\">as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She was studying for her test <span class =\"strong\">when</span> I called her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">While</span> I was opening the cupboard, I heard a loud crash.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">As</span> I was walking, the bird flew by.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to catch up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk to someone and find out what they have been doing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to catch up soon!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about free activities. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to paint your nails", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put color on your fingernails", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was painting my nails.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bring over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take something from one place to another place where someone else is, especially their home", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll bring over a pizza to your place tonight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to gaze", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at someone or something for a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did he gaze into your eyes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "each other", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to show that one person does something with the other ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(pronoun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you talk to each other?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mood", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way you feel about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You always ruin my happy mood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "give a call", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to call someone using the telephone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll give you a call when I have time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of your last birthday. What did you do?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short summary (7-8 sentences) about this event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your summary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read it aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to their summary.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about an event in the past. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I was doing when something else happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about events in the past.", "type": "text"}]}]}